>         /// After parsing, <see cref="Parent"/> is the node in the tree that has this node as or in <see cref="Children"/>.

Might be overkill here, but perhaps we can consider adding a sample pattern and a sample tree on this remarks in order to get a better picture of what the tree/Parent structure looks like? For example, we could do something simple like:

```c#
/// For example, for the pattern (a(b|c))* the following tree would be generated:
/// - Loop Node
///   - Capture Node 1
///     - Concat Node
///       - One Node 'a'
///       - Capture Node 2
///         - Alternation Node
///           - One Node 'b'
///           - One Node 'c'
```

I know that the above example probably wouldn't look like that after optimizing it, but my point is just if we are doing remarks we might want to add an example. As I said this might be overkill so up-to you if you want to add it, and don't reset CI for this, I can add these docs later as well.

